# Popup Outside-Action Dismissal

Any popup menu, picker, tooltip-like action panel, or floating control sheet must
close when the user performs a pointer action outside its owning control and
popup. This applies to Web and PWA UI, including audio volume and playback-speed
menus.

Requirements:

- Register a document-level `pointerdown` or equivalent outside-action listener
  only while the popup is open.
- Keep the listener in capture mode when needed so the popup closes before
  unrelated underlying controls process the action.
- Do not close when the event target is inside the popup/trigger wrapper.
- Always remove the listener on close and component unmount.
- Preserve existing timeout dismissal, if any; outside action is an additional
  dismissal path.

```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  if (!open) return
  const closeOutside = (event: PointerEvent) => {
    const target = event.target
    if (target instanceof Node && ownerRef.current?.contains(target)) return
    setOpen(false)
  }
  document.addEventListener('pointerdown', closeOutside, true)
  return () => document.removeEventListener('pointerdown', closeOutside, true)
}, [open])
```

Do not use a permanent document listener, and do not close a popup for actions
inside its own slider, buttons, or menu items.
